        "# 3. Data preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "Check for missing values and duplicates. Define the 30 input features (X) and the diagnosis (y), then split the data into 80% training and 20% testing. Stratification preserves the class proportions in both groups. Scaling is unnecessary for a decision tree."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eMnTRDCSPKXf"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(\"Missing values:\", data.isnull().sum().sum())\n",
        "print(\"Duplicate rows:\", data.duplicated().sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "# Drop duplicates if any exist; no records are removed from this dataset.\n",
        "data = data.drop_duplicates().copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# This built-in dataset has no missing values. Raise an error if this changes.\n",
        "assert not data.isnull().any().any(), \"Unexpected missing values in the dataset.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "X = data.drop(columns=[\"diagnosis\"])\n",
        "y = data[\"diagnosis\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=42, stratify=y\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Training samples:\", len(X_train))\n",
        "print(\"Testing samples:\", len(X_test))\n",
        "print(\"Number of features:\", X.shape[1])\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ldocQvJbPKha",
        "outputId": "5bcf91de-2caf-46ae-d8af-d288c5376991"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Missing values: 0\n",
            "Duplicate rows: 0\n",
            "Training samples: 455\n",
            "Testing samples: 114\n",
            "Number of features: 30\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**4. Model selection and training**\n",
        "\n",
        "Use a DecisionTreeClassifier with max_depth=4 to obtain an interpretable tree and reduce the risk of overfitting. Set random_state=42 for reproducible results. Train the model using only the training data."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "06MYLTiMPKzT"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "model = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=4, random_state=42)\n",
        "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Decision tree trained successfully.\")\n",
        "print(\"Tree depth:\", model.get_depth())\n",
        "print(\"Number of leaves:\", model.get_n_leaves())"
